      "message": "```\n#include \u003czephyr/sys/util.h\u003e\n\n/* Zephyr definition */\n#define ROUND_UP(x, align) \\\n    ((((unsigned long)(x) + ((unsigned long)(align) - 1)) / (unsigned long)(align)) * \\\n    (unsigned long)(align))\n```\n\nKey Differences \u0026 Compiler Optimization\n\n- Mathematical vs. Bitwise: Your ALIGN_UP macro uses bitwise \u0026 math, which only works if align is a power of 2. Zephyr\u0027s ROUND_UP uses mathematical division and multiplication, allowing it to work with any alignment value.\n\n- Optimization: You don\u0027t have to worry about the performance penalty of division; if align is a power of 2 known at compile-time, modern compilers (like GCC and Clang used in the Zephyr SDK) will automatically optimize ROUND_UP into the exact same bitwise mask operations (\u0026 ~(align - 1)) you wrote.",
